# Detection 1: Failed Logon Brute Force
# MITRE ATT&CK: T1110 (Brute Force)
# Data Source: WinEventLog:Security, EventCode 4625
#
# Logic: Bucket failed logon events into 5-minute windows and surface
# any host where 5+ failures occurred within a single window. The
# values() aggregation captures which account names were targeted,
# which is essential triage context for the analyst.
#
# False-positive considerations: Service accounts with stale cached
# credentials and users locked out after password changes can both
# trigger this. Tune by excluding known service account names.

index=main sourcetype=WinEventLog:Security EventCode=4625
| bucket _time span=5m
| stats count AS failed_logons, values(Account_Name) AS accounts_targeted by _time, host
| where failed_logons >= 5